    {
      "title": "Shell vs Environment Variables: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Shell vs Environment Variables: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two kinds of variable",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Shell variable}: lives only in the ==current shell process==",
                "Set with `NAME=value` (==no spaces== around `=`), read with `$NAME`",
                "{green:Environment variable}: a shell variable ==marked for export==",
                "Copied into the environment of ==every child process== the shell starts"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Inheritance is one-way",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Parent shell",
                    "sub": "exported vars",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fork/exec",
                    "sub": "snapshot copy",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Child process",
                    "sub": "own copy",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Child gets a ==snapshot== at fork/exec",
                "Child's changes ==never flow back== to the parent"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Unexported `FOO` is invisible to the child; after `export` it is inherited"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "FOO=1; bash -c 'echo $FOO'",
                "export FOO; bash -c 'echo $FOO'"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "",
                "1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No spaces around =",
              "text": "`FOO = 1` runs a command named ==FOO== with args `=` and `1`: **command not found**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "export and Setting Variables for One Command",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "export and Setting Variables for One Command",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. export",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`export NAME=value` ==sets and exports== in one step",
                "`export NAME` exports an existing shell variable",
                "`export -n NAME` removes the export flag",
                "Changes reach ==only children started afterwards==; running processes keep their old copy"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. One-shot prefix",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`NAME=value cmd` puts NAME in ==cmd's environment only==",
                "The shell's own variable stays unchanged"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Prefix",
                "export"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Lasts",
                  "one command",
                  "rest of the session"
                ],
                [
                  "Reaches",
                  "that command",
                  "all later children"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "FOO=1 sh -c 'echo $FOO'",
                "echo \"[$FOO]\""
              ],
              "note": "FOO was not set before"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "1",
                "[]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes and unset",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "FOO=1 echo $FOO prints empty",
              "text": "The shell expands `$FOO` ==before== the prefix applies. Use `FOO=1 sh -c 'echo $FOO'`."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`unset NAME` ==removes== the variable entirely",
                "`NAME=` only sets it ==empty== (still defined)"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "PATH Lookup, which and type",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "PATH Lookup, which and type",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. How the Shell Finds a Command",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`PATH` is a ==colon-separated== list of directories",
                "Searched {blue:left to right}; the first executable match runs",
                "A name containing `/` skips PATH"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Alias",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Function",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Builtin",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "PATH search",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. type vs which",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Shows",
                "Misses"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`type cmd`",
                  "alias, builtin, function or file",
                  "nothing"
                ],
                [
                  "`type -a cmd`",
                  "all matches, in order",
                  "nothing"
                ],
                [
                  "`command -v cmd`",
                  "how it resolves",
                  "nothing"
                ],
                [
                  "`which cmd`",
                  "PATH programs only",
                  "aliases, builtins"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Editing PATH",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "export PATH=\"$PATH:/new/dir\"  # append: lowest priority",
                "PATH=\"/new/dir:$PATH\"         # prepend: overrides",
                "hash -r  # clear cached locations"
              ],
              "note": "run hash -r after installing or moving a binary"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`export PATH=/new/dir` overwrites PATH, so `ls` breaks",
                "Trailing or empty PATH entry means the ==current directory==",
                "A local script needs `./script`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "In scripts",
              "text": "Use `type` or `command -v`, not `which`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Startup Files: ~/.bashrc vs ~/.profile",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Startup Files: ~/.bashrc vs ~/.profile",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Which file is read",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Shell",
                "Example",
                "Reads"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Login==",
                  "SSH, console, `bash -l`",
                  "/etc/profile, then first of ~/.bash_profile, ~/.bash_login, ~/.profile"
                ],
                [
                  "==Interactive non-login==",
                  "new tab, `bash`",
                  "~/.bashrc only"
                ],
                [
                  "==Non-interactive==",
                  "a script",
                  "neither; inherits parent's environment"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Convention and the fix",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==~/.profile==: exported variables and PATH (once per login)",
                "==~/.bashrc==: aliases, prompt, functions (every interactive shell)",
                "Split problem: login shells never read ~/.bashrc",
                "Fix: ~/.profile or ~/.bash_profile {blue:sources} ~/.bashrc"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "# in ~/.profile",
                "[ -f ~/.bashrc ] && . ~/.bashrc"
              ],
              "note": "login shells now get aliases too"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Reload and PATH mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Edits skip the open shell: `source ~/.bashrc` or `. ~/.bashrc`",
                "Or open a new shell; ~/.profile changes need ==re-login==",
                "Unguarded PATH append in ~/.bashrc grows PATH on every nested shell or re-source"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Guard the append",
              "text": "Add the directory only if PATH lacks it:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "case \":$PATH:\" in *\":$HOME/bin:\"*) ;;",
                "  *) PATH=\"$PATH:$HOME/bin\" ;;",
                "esac"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "env, printenv and sudo with the Environment",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "env, printenv and sudo with the Environment",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Reading the environment",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Shows"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`printenv`",
                  "exported variables"
                ],
                [
                  "`printenv NAME`",
                  "one value, no `$`; {red:exit 1} if unset"
                ],
                [
                  "`env`",
                  "same list as `printenv`"
                ],
                [
                  "`set`",
                  "also shell variables and functions"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Changing it for one command",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`env` runs a command with an ==adjusted environment==",
                "`-i` starts empty; `-u` removes one variable"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "env DEBUG=1 cmd",
                "env -i cmd",
                "env -u HOME cmd"
              ],
              "note": "extra variable / empty environment / one removed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. sudo and the environment",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "sudo ==resets== the environment (`env_reset`): most variables dropped",
                "PATH becomes {blue:secure_path} from sudoers"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`sudo VAR=value cmd` passes one variable",
                "`sudo -E cmd` keeps yours, still limited by sudoers policy",
                "`sudo env PATH=\"$PATH\" cmd` carries your PATH"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Tool in your PATH gives {red:command not found} under sudo: use the ==full path==",
                "`sudo echo $HOME` expands in your shell first; use `sudo sh -c 'echo $HOME'`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Variables, PATH and Startup Files",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Variables, PATH and Startup Files",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Set and Inspect",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Scope"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`VAR=v`",
                  "shell only"
                ],
                [
                  "`export VAR=v`",
                  "inherited by children"
                ],
                [
                  "`VAR=v cmd`",
                  "one command"
                ],
                [
                  "`unset VAR`",
                  "removes it"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`printenv VAR`: one exported value",
                "`env`: all exported variables",
                "`set`: shell variables too",
                "`echo \"$VAR\"`: expanded value"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. PATH and Resolve",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "export PATH=\"$PATH:/dir\"   # append",
                "PATH=\"/dir:$PATH\"          # prepend",
                "echo \"$PATH\" | tr : '\\n'   # one per line"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`type -a cmd`: all matches in order",
                "`command -v cmd`: script-safe lookup",
                "`which cmd`: PATH only, misses aliases",
                "`hash -r`: clear cached locations"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Startup and sudo",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Login: `/etc/profile` + `~/.profile`",
                "Interactive non-login: `~/.bashrc`",
                "Reload: `source ~/.bashrc`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "sudo: env reset + =={secure_path}==",
                "Pass vars: `sudo VAR=v cmd`, `sudo -E`, full paths",
                "`sudo sh -c '...'` expands inside root"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Expands first",
              "text": "`sudo echo $HOME` expands in **your** shell before sudo runs."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "With FOO unset, what does `FOO=1 echo $FOO` print?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "An empty line.",
                "The shell expands `$FOO` before the prefix applies; use `FOO=1 sh -c 'echo $FOO'`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You run `PATH=/opt/bin` and then `ls`. What happens, and why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`ls: command not found`.",
                "It overwrote PATH, so `/bin` and `/usr/bin` are no longer searched. Use `PATH=\"$PATH:/opt/bin\"`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`mytool` lives in `~/bin`, which is on your PATH, but `sudo mytool` says command not found. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "sudo resets PATH to `secure_path`, which ignores yours.",
                "Use the full path or `sudo env PATH=\"$PATH\" mytool`."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}